1
00:00:08,851 --> 00:00:12,914
Medicine ki MRP mein GST pehle se shaamil hota
hai.

2
00:00:12,954 --> 00:00:17,259
Medoro har bill par MRP se taxable value
nikaalta hai,

3
00:00:17,299 --> 00:00:24,259
aur Jharkhand ke andar ki bikri par GST ko CGST
aur SGST mein aadha-aadha baant'ta hai.

4
00:00:24,299 --> 00:00:28,523
Doosre rajya ke GST wale customer par IGST lagta
hai.

5
00:00:29,271 --> 00:00:34,464
Har medicine ka HSN code aur GST rate uske
master mein rehta hai,

6
00:00:34,504 --> 00:00:36,799
jaise medicines ke liye 3004.

7
00:00:36,839 --> 00:00:41,468
'Reports & GST' screen par GST returns wala
hissa dekhiye.

8
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:43,888
GST month chuniye.

9
00:00:43,928 --> 00:00:50,861
Medoro us mahine ke bills se GSTR-1 banata hai:
B2B, B2C aur HSN summary,

10
00:00:50,901 --> 00:00:55,063
section-wise taxable value aur tax ke saath.

11
00:00:55,807 --> 00:01:03,171
Yahan se GSTR-1 JSON, jo GST portal ke offline
tool mein jaata hai, HSN summary CSV,

12
00:01:03,211 --> 00:01:07,313
aur GSTR-3B ke JSON aur CSV download hote hain.

13
00:01:08,078 --> 00:01:10,513
Aapka CA Tally istemaal karta hai?

14
00:01:10,553 --> 00:01:18,084
'Books & registers' mein Tally export se Tally
Prime ke liye XML banta hai: pehle ledgers yaani
masters,

15
00:01:18,124 --> 00:01:19,103
phir vouchers.

16
00:01:19,143 --> 00:01:24,708
Tally mein Import karte hi bikri, khareed,
payments aur kharch aa jaate hain,

17
00:01:24,748 --> 00:01:27,984
har customer aur supplier ke ledger ke saath.

18
00:01:28,757 --> 00:01:33,602
Bahut zaroori: yeh reports aur exports filing
mein madad ke liye hain.

19
00:01:33,642 --> 00:01:39,603
GST return file karne se pehle inhein apne
accountant ya CA se zaroor check karvaaiye.
